WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.735
Since we're talking about January six,

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:04.771
I do want to take you back to that day.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.240
Take a look at the video over here.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.341
That, of course, was the news

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.009
hanging outside

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:09.542
the Capitol

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.143
that day

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:10.844
and rioters

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.313
were calling for your execution,

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.148
chanting Hang Mike Pence

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.683
almost two years later.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.251
Is it still tough to hear

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.886
some of the video of the hang Mike Pence

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.321
two years later?

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.722
Is it still tough to see that

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:23.623
and hear that

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:30.063
Jake, it saddens me

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.632
but that day it angered me

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.735
I must tell you, when

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.472
when the Secret Service took us down

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.074
to the loading dock,

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.542
accompanied by my wife,

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:42.976
my daughter

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:45.378
Charlotte, and our Secret Service detail

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.081
I was determined to stay at my post.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:51.117
I told the Secret Service that I

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.285
was not leaving the Capitol.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.621
I didn't want to give those people

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:55.555
the sight of a six

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:56.322
car motorcade

00:00:56.322 --> 00:01:00.226
speeding away from the Capitol that day.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.763
But frankly, when I saw those images

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.032
and when when I read

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:09.002
a tweet that President Trump issued

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.603
saying that I lack courage

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.172
in that moment.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.005
Well,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.109
it angered me greatly.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:16.943
But to be honest with you,

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.812
I didn't have time for it.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.581
President had decided in that moment

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.682
to be a part of the problem.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.150
I decided

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:24.984
and was determined

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:27.387
to be part of the solution.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:30.190
And so we essentially set that aside.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.492
I collected the Republican

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.026
and Democrat

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:33.893
leadership of the House

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.295
and Senate on a conference call,

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.564
and we began to work the problem.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.934
They tasked me to reach out

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.202
to leadership at the Pentagon,

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.170
the leadership of the Justice Department

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.106
to surge additional resources there.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.408
And thanks to the courage of those

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.543
amazing Capitol Hill police officers

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.279
and federal law enforcement,

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.248
we would quell the violence.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.583
We reconvened

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:59.319
the Congress the very same day.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.354
And I'll always believe that

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.890
because of their courage and valor,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.093
a day of tragedy became

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.561
a triumph of freedom.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.563
We demonstrated to the American people

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.899
and the world the strength

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:13.933
of our institutions,

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.969
the resilience of our democracy.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.437
But those memories

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:19.205
those images will always be with me.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:22.108
So you just said that the president

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.877
in that moment decided

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.345
to be part of the problem.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.613
And I have to say, as somebody

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.648
that had been reporting on it

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.851
for the months leading up to January six,

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.019
I don't think anything happened

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:33.887
in that moment.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.088
That was part of the problem.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.123
President Trump had been

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.260
campaigning

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.161
in favor

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.295
of the overturning of the election

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.063
for months and months and months.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.365
It wasn't in that moment

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.766
and he wasn't part of the problem.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.001
He was the problem.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:50.937
Well, look, the

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:51.337
the people

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.505
who rioted at the Capitol

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.574
are responsible for what they did.

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:55.942
And as I said that day,

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.278
and I believe every day since.

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:00.613
Well, those people should be prosecuted

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:03.183
to the fullest extent of the law.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.818
When I saw the images of people

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:08.955
smashing windows ransacking offices

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.823
and creating the mayhem

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.393
that ultimately cost lives.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.595
I was filled with a simmering indignation

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.698
that served in the Congress for 12 years.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.999
I dreamed

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:20.500
from the time

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.301
I was a little boy,

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.002
as I wrote in my book about someday

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.737
representing my hometown in Congress

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.307
and to see what was happening there

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.042
The first time since 1814

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:31.244
at our Capitol building, I,

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:34.214
I just found myself thinking not this,

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:37.317
not here, not in America.

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.419
And I hear you loud and clear.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.053
Look there.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:41.988
In the weeks

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.890
after the election, I had,

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.025
I told the President

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:48.728
that after all the legal challenges

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.530
would play out,

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.331
which the campaign

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.299
had every right to bring. Sure.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.334
I mean, there were,

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.501
Jake, voting

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.303
irregularity is in a number of states

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.871
where election laws

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.039
had been changed by either

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:02.475
executive action or by the courts.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.077
There was never evidence

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.044
of widespread fraud.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:05.979
I don't believe

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:06.746
fraud changed

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.514
the outcome of the election.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.449
But

00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:11.618
the president and the campaign

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.752
had every right

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.153
to have those examined in court.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.022
But I told the president

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:16.823
that once

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.391
those legal challenges played out,

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.692
he should
simply accept

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:22.695
the outcome of the election and move on.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.697
But he was hearing different voices

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:27.500
and frankly, there were

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.069
there were some legal experts that

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:30.870
that were allowed on the

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.205
White House grounds that

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:34.207
there should have never

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.108
been let through the gate

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.542
And you're talking about Sidney Powell.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.310
Rudy Giuliani.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.611
I want to come back to that in a second.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.613
But I do want to show this moment

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:41.914
because it was so important

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.416
and so heartbreaking.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.885
This is inside the Capitol.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.153
This is video of the Secret Service

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:48.721
trying to get you and your wife, Karen,

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:51.190
and your daughter, Charlotte, to safety

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.126
as rioters came within 40 feet of you.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.161
We found out later

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.930
your family's lives were at risk,

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.132
not just yours,

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.266
although that would be tragic,

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.035
but your wife's and your daughters.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:04.237
And I was worried for you that day, sir.

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:05.571
Covering this.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:06.606
I was worried for your wife.

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:08.374
I was worried for your daughter

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.009
and relieved that nobody was harmed

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:11.877
you.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.614
If I were you, I would

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:17.684
still be livid with Donald Trump.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.887
I would be so furious.

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:25.525
And I know you're a measured man.

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:29.162
But are you still angry

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.399
Well, I must tell you, the president's

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:37.470
words and tweet that day were reckless.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:41.641
They endangered my family and

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:44.310
and all the people at the Capitol.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.379
And I was angry.

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:48.181
But, you know, my Christian faith

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.850
tells me to be quick to listen,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:54.320
slow to speak and slow to become angry.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.355
And in the Christian faith,

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:57.657
forgiveness is not optional.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.492
We literally pray in the Lord's Prayer

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.661
to forgive those who trespass against us.

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:04.230
And in the days that followed,

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.865
when the president asked to meet with me

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.300
after he made the right

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.534
statements to the country

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.535
committed to a peaceful

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.070
transfer of power, he'd

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.272
condemn the people that rioted

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.173
at the Capitol

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:19.746
We met, we sat down and I prayed.

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.148
I prayed for God's

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:24.350
grace to meet that moment in that spirit.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:27.153
And it wasn't easy.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:27.920
And

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:31.657
I and to be honest with you, I'm

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.659
I'm as human as the next guy.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:34.660
And I,

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.963
I still pray for the president,

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.197
and I pray for the grace

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:40.299
to forgive him and all those responsible

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.835
for that tragic day.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:45.004
But, well,

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:47.707
I truly do believe that we live in a time

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:48.741
when the American people ought

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:50.710
to be searching our hearts

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:54.714
and having more grace toward one another.

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:56.916
And it seems like

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:58.584
our country is more divided

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:01.087
now than ever before.

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:03.723
Even broadcast networks seem to be

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.958
perceived to be divided along

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:06.926
partizan lines,

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.661
which is why I'm grateful

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.797
for the opportunity to be on CNN today.

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:13.733
I just think if

00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:16.202
if all of us can be more forgiving

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:19.272
to one another, will

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:20.840
we'll have unity in this country

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.475
more than we've had in recent years.

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:25.545
And and with that, unity will meet

00:07:25.545 --> 00:07:27.180
the challenges that America faces

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:28.614
in the balance of this new century.

